WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:07.500
There are many ways in which, we can find the HCF of two numbers.

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.920
But in this video,

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.460
we will look at the Prime Factor Method.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.560
Let's say we want to find the 'HCF' of 24 and 36.

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:19.400
What we need to do is very simple.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.280
We just have to reduce the numbers to its Prime Factors.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.900
And we can do that using Upside-Down Division.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.740
First, let's find the Prime Factors of 24.

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.320
We draw two lines like these.

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:37.440
Now we think of all the Prime Factors that 24 is divisible by.

00:00:37.880 --> 00:00:39.880
We start with 2.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:47.160
24 is divisible by 2, so we write a 2 here. 2 times 12 is 24.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.720
What about 12? Is it divisible by 2?

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.040
Yes, 12 is also divisible by 2.

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.160
We write 2 again and draw a line.

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.440
2 times 6 is 12.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:04.500
6 is also divisible by 2 and 2 times 3 is 6.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:08.520
We stop here, as we got a Prime Factor.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.820
How can we write 24 now?

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:13.060
Remember the L-Shape.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:18.940
24 can be written as 2 x 2 x 2 x 3.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.280
We reduce 24 to its Prime Factors.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.960
We do the same for 36.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:29.800
Actually, why don't you try reducing 36 to its Prime Factors?

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.640
Pause the video and give it a shot.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:43.600
36 is divisible by 2 and 2 times 18 is 36.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:49.100
18 is also divisible by 2 and 2 times 9 is 18.

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.640
Is 9 divisible by 2?

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.440
No, 9 is not divisible by 2.

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:57.800
And we jump to the next Prime number which is 3.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:03.260
Is 9 divisible by 3? Yes, 9 is divisible by 3

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.840
3 times 3 is 9.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:09.040
We stop here since it's a prime Factor.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:13.340
36 can be written as the product of these 4 numbers.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:19.220
36 is equal to 2 x 2 x 3 x 3.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.580
The difficult part is over.

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.740
But how does this give us the HCF?

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:26.900
To find the HCF,

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:29.720
all we have to do is multiply the Prime Factors,

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:32.840
that are common to both the numbers.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:37.940
2 is a common Prime Factor to both the numbers, so we write a 2 once.

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:40.540
There is another 2 that is common to both.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.520
So we multiply this 2 with another 2.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:47.600
And there is a 3 which is common to both the numbers as well.

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:51.020
Hence we multiply this product with 3.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.080
Yes, we just multiplied the Prime Factors,

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:56.680
which are common to both the numbers.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:59.380
This gives us the HCF.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:04.020
2 times 2 is 4 and 4 times 3 is 12.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:09.440
The Highest Common Factor of 24 and 36 is 12.

00:03:09.640 --> 00:03:11.460
This is the Prime Factor Method

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.960
to find the Highest Common Factor of two numbers.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:20.740
In the next session we will solve for the HCF of 42 and 56.

